text:
In the deep blue sea,
Whale sings to the walnut tree;
Nature’s melody. 

Under the vast sky,
Walnut tree whispers secrets;
Whale dances in joy.

Ancient whale, wise soul,
Beside you, the sturdy oak;
Nature's grand ballet.

Whale breaches the waves,
Leaves swirl from the walnut tree;
Nature's harmony.

In the ocean's heart,
Whale's song merges with the tree;
A world in balance.

The whale swims below,
While the walnut tree waves hello;
Connected by breeze. 

Walnut tree stands tall,
Whale's song carried on the wind;
Nature's silent pact.

Beneath the walnut,
Whale dreams of the sunlit world;
A peaceful coexistence. 

Whale glides, tree sways,
In a rhythm understood,
By the language of nature. 

Beneath the walnut,
Whale finds solace in the deep;
Nature's gentle embrace.
